PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
Due to the Labor Day holiday, a meeting of the Public Services Committee was instead held on
Tuesday, September 2, 2025, in Council Chambers and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00
p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS:
Jeff White, Acting Chairman; Dr. Michelle Aldrich; Dr. Kathy
Emmons; and Dr. Mark Rinne. Absent: Tom Segrave, Chairman.
AGENDA ITEMS
6.
ORDINANCE
— 3 READING
—
Annexing to the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, land
northeast of the intersection of Frontier Mali Drive and Rue Terre Avenue and west of
Converse Avenue.
Dr. Emmons moved to approve on 3”' and final reading, seconded by Dr. Aldrich. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department Senior Planner, provided a staff report and
committee member Aldrich commented on the item.
7.
ORDINANCE
3”' READING
— Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne, establishing the zoning classification of CB
— Community Business for land
annexed to the City of Cheyenne located northeast of the intersection of Frontier Mall
Drive and Rue Terre Avenue and west of Converse Avenue.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 3’ and final reading, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department Senior Planner, provided a staff report.
8.
ORDINANCE 3t1 READING
— Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne, changing the zoning classification for land located southwest of the intersection
of holland Court and Ridge Road from
AG
— Agricultural to NR-2
— Neighborhood
Residential
— Medium Density.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 3”' and final reading, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department Senior Planner, provided a staff report.
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
9.
ORDINANCE —2”’ READING — Creating Section 10.24.200, Vehicle Mufflers, Excessive
Smoke and Unreasonable Noise, and repealing Section 8.56.050, Motor Vehicle Mufflers,
of the Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, to revise and enhance
provisions governing vehicle mufflers and noise, to establish a graduated penalty structure
for recurring offenses, and to make conforming amendments as specified. (POSTPONED
FROM AUGUST 25, 2025)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 2 reading, seconded by Dr. Rinne. Dr. Aldrich moved to amend
section 10.24.200(DX5) to read “The operation of a vehicle with equipment improperly installed
or removed so as to produce unreasonable noise. This includes, but is not limited to unlawful,
defective or modified exhaust systems, vehicles lacking a functioning muffler or exhaust system.”
Seconded by Dr. Rinne. Motion to amend failed with Dr. Emmons and Dr. Rinne voting “NO”
and Dr. Aldrich voting “YES.” The main motion was approved by unanimous voice vote.
John Brodie, City Attorney, provided a staff report and Captain David Janes, Police Department,
provided additional information related to the enforcement of the current versus the proposed
ordinance.
All committee members commented on the item, as did Ward I Councilman Pete
Labyourn.
There being no further items for the agenda to come before the Public Services Committee, the
meeting was adjourned at 12:40 p.m.
Submitted by,
‘tM/aaeb
Jennifer McClelland
Executive Assistant to the Cheyenne City Council
```
